      "mergeID": "5f0ca7e73c50946d7f0ec4aa",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Say that your viewpoint is 0.1 units above the location of your head bone. If an animation changes the y-axis scale of the head bone from 1 to 0.9 and you use Animator Set View to set the view point to the head, does the position of your viewpoint stay 0.1 units above the head bone or does it change to 0.09 units above the head bone?\nAlthough it should change to 0.09 to remain at the right part of your head, it currently stays at 0.1. This means that changing the scale of the head bone by a significant amount will cause the viewpoint to either raise or lower from its intended position.\nHere is a link to a video showing this bug in practice: https://youtu.be/bilvh2cnGPQ",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[Bug] Animator Set View does not account for changing the scale of the head bone.",
